(sanguine a statement of future possibilities in political practice,) Tj T*
(let him consider how absurd it would have appeared in the days of) Tj T*
(Edward I. if the present state of social economy had been then) Tj T*
(predicted as necessary, or even described as possible. And I believe) Tj T*
(the advance from the days of Edward I. to our own, great as it is) Tj T*
(confessedly, consists, not so much in what we have actually) Tj T*
(accomplished, as in what we are now enabled to conceive.) Tj T*
