(Now, you must have patience with me, if in approaching the specialty) Tj T*
(of this subject, I dwell a little on certain points of general) Tj T*
(political science already known or established: for though thus, as I) Tj T*
(believe, established, some which I shall have occasion to rest) Tj T*
(arguments on are not yet by any means universally accepted; and) Tj T*
(therefore, though I will not lose time in any detailed defence of) Tj T*
(them, it is necessary that I should distinctly tell you in what form I) Tj T*
(receive, and wish to argue from them; and this the more, because there) Tj T*
(may perhaps be a part of my audience who have not interested) Tj T*
(themselves in political economy, as it bears on ordinary fields of) Tj T*
(labour, but may yet wish to hear in what way its principles can be) Tj T*
(applied to Art. I shall, therefore, take leave to trespass on your) Tj T*
(patience with a few elementary statements in the outset, and with, the) Tj T*
(expression of some general principles, here and there, in the course) Tj T*
(of our particular inquiry.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(To begin, then, with one of these necessary truisms: all economy,) Tj T*
(whether of states, households, or individuals, may be defined to be) Tj T*
(the art of managing labour. The world is so regulated by the laws of) Tj T*
(Providence, that a man's labour, well applied, is always amply) Tj T*
(sufficient to provide him during his life with all things needful to) Tj T*
(him, and not only with those, but with many pleasant objects of) Tj T*
(luxury; and yet farther, to procure him large intervals of healthful) Tj T*
(rest and serviceable leisure. And a nation's labour, well applied, is) Tj T*
(in like manner, amply sufficient to provide its whole population with) Tj T*
(good food and comfortable habitation; and not with those only, but) Tj T*
(with good education besides, and objects of luxury, art treasures,) Tj T*
(such as these you have around you now. But by those same laws of) Tj T*
(Nature and Providence, if the labour of the nation or of the) Tj T*
(individual be misapplied, and much more if it be insufficient,--if the) Tj T*
(nation or man be indolent and unwise,--suffering and want result,) Tj T*
(exactly in proportion to the indolence and improvidence,--to the) Tj T*
(refusal of labour, or to the misapplication of it. Wherever you see) Tj T*
(want, or misery, or degradation, in this world about you, there, be) Tj T*
(sure, either industry has been wanting, or industry has been in error.) Tj T*
(It is not accident, it is not Heaven-commanded calamity, it is not the) Tj T*
(original and inevitable evil of man's nature, which fill your streets) Tj T*
(with lamentation, and your graves with prey. It is only that, when) Tj T*
(there should have been providence, there has been waste; when there) Tj T*
(should have been labour, there has been lasciviousness; and,) Tj T*
(wilfulness, when there should have been subordination.[2]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(    [2] Proverbs xiii. 23: "Much food is in the tillage of the poor:) Tj T*
(        but there is that is destroyed for want of judgment.") Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Now, we have warped the word "economy" in our English: language into a) Tj T*
(meaning which it has no business whatever to bear. In our use of it,) Tj T*
(it constantly signifies merely sparing or saving; economy of money) Tj T*
(means saving money--economy of time, sparing time, and so on. But that) Tj T*
(is a wholly barbarous use of the word--barbarous in a double sense,) Tj T*
