() Tj T*
(A. Their power of SELECTION relates to things of which the supply is) Tj T*
(limited \(as the supply of best things is always\). When it becomes) Tj T*
(matter of question to whom such things are to belong, the richest) Tj T*
(person has necessarily the first choice, unless some arbitrary mode of) Tj T*
(distribution be otherwise determined upon. The business of the) Tj T*
(economist is to show how this choice may be a Wise one.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(B. Their power of DIRECTION arises out of the necessary relation of) Tj T*
(rich men to poor, which ultimately, in one way or another, involves) Tj T*
(the direction of, or authority over, the labour of the poor; and this) Tj T*
(nearly as much over their mental as their bodily labour. The business) Tj T*
(of the economist is to show how this direction may be a Just one.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
