() Tj T*
(For example, let us imagine a society, of no great extent, occupied in) Tj T*
(procuring and laying up store of corn, wine, wool, silk, and other) Tj T*
(such preservable materials of food and clothing; and that it has a) Tj T*
(currency representing them. Imagine farther, that on days of) Tj T*
(festivity, the society, discovering itself to derive satisfaction from) Tj T*
(pyrotechnics, gradually turns its attention more and more to the) Tj T*
(manufacture of gunpowder; so that an increasing number of labourers,) Tj T*
(giving what time they can spare to this branch of industry, bring) Tj T*
(increasing quantities of combustibles into the store, and use the) Tj T*
(general orders received in exchange to obtain such wine, wool, or corn) Tj T*
(as they may have need of. The currency remains the same, and) Tj T*
(represents precisely the same amount of material in the store, and of) Tj T*
(labour spent in producing it. But the corn and wine gradually vanish,) Tj T*
(and in their place, as gradually, appear sulphur and saltpetre; till) Tj T*
(at last, the labourers who have consumed corn and supplied nitre,) Tj T*
(presenting on a festal morning some of their currency to obtain) Tj T*
(materials for the feast, discover that no amount of currency will) Tj T*
(command anything Festive, except Fire. The supply of rockets is) Tj T*
(unlimited, but that of food limited in a quite final manner; and the) Tj T*
(whole currency in the hands of the society represents an infinite) Tj T*
(power of detonation, but none of existence.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The statement, caricatured as it may seem, is only exaggerated in) Tj T*
(assuming the persistence of the folly to extremity, unchecked, as in) Tj T*
(reality it would be, by the gradual rise in price of food. But it) Tj T*
(falls short of the actual facts of human life in expression of the) Tj T*
(depth and intensity of the folly itself. For a great part \(the reader) Tj T*
(would not believe how great until he saw the statistics in detail\) of) Tj T*
(the most earnest and ingenious industry of the world is spent in) Tj T*
(producing munitions of war; gathering that is to say the materials,) Tj T*
(not of festive, but of consuming fire; filling its stores with all) Tj T*
(power of the instruments of pain, and all affluence of the ministries) Tj T*
(of death. It was no true Trionfo della Morte which men have seen and) Tj T*
(feared \(sometimes scarcely feared\) so long;--wherein he brought them) Tj T*
(rest from their labours. We see and share another and higher form of) Tj T*
