(place cheapest; and it becomes often desirable that products raised in) Tj T*
(one country should be wrought in another. Hence have arisen) Tj T*
(discussions on "International values," which will be one day) Tj T*
(remembered as highly curious exercises of the human mind. For it will) Tj T*
(be discovered, in due course of tide and time, that international) Tj T*
(value is regulated just as inter-provincial or inter-parishional value) Tj T*
(is. Coals and hops are exchanged between Northumberland and Kent on) Tj T*
(absolutely the same principles as iron and wine between Lancashire and) Tj T*
(Spain. The greater breadth of an arm of the sea increases the cost,) Tj T*
(but does not modify the principle of exchange; and a bargain written) Tj T*
(in two languages will have no other economical results than a bargain) Tj T*
(written in one. The distances of nations are measured not by seas, but) Tj T*
(by ignorances; and their divisions determined, not by dialects, but by) Tj T*
(enmities.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
