(relation in its simplest elements in order to reach its first) Tj T*
(principles. The simplest state of it is, then, this:[115] a wise and) Tj T*
(provident person works much, consumes little, and lays by store; an) Tj T*
(improvident person works little, consumes all the produce, and lays by) Tj T*
(no store. Accident interrupts the daily work, or renders it less) Tj T*
(productive; the idle person must then starve, or be supported by the) Tj T*
(provident one,--who, having him thus at his mercy, may either refuse) Tj T*
(to maintain him altogether, or, which will evidently be more to his) Tj T*
(own interest, say to him, "I will maintain you, indeed, but you shall) Tj T*
