endobj
458 0 obj
<< /Length 3390 >>
stream
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 738 Td 13 TL
(     more than one word, after the junction--a word as it were of) Tj T*
(     many waters, sometimes both sweet and bitter. Thus the whole) Tj T*
(     force of our English "charity" depends on the guttural in) Tj T*
(     "Charis" getting confused with the "c" of the Latin "carus;") Tj T*
(     thenceforward throughout the middle ages, the two ideas) Tj T*
(     ran on together, and both got confused with St. Paul's) Tj T*
(     [Greek: agape], which expresses a different idea in all) Tj T*
(     sorts of ways; our "charity," having not only brought in the) Tj T*
(     entirely foreign sense of almsgiving, but lost the essential) Tj T*
(     sense of contentment, and lost much more in getting too far) Tj T*
(     away from the "charis," of the final Gospel benedictions.) Tj T*
(     For truly it is fine Christianity we have come to, which) Tj T*
(     professing to expect the perpetual grace of its Founder,) Tj T*
(     has not itself grace enough to save it from overreaching) Tj T*
(     its friends in sixpenny bargains; and which, supplicating) Tj T*
(     evening and morning the forgiveness of its own debts, goes) Tj T*
(     forth in the daytime to take its fellow-servants by the) Tj T*
(     throat, saying--not "Pay me that thou owest," but "Pay me) Tj T*
(     that thou owest me not.") Tj T*
() Tj T*
(     Not but that we sometimes wear Ophelia's rue with a) Tj T*
(     difference, and call it, "Herb o' grace o' Sundays," taking) Tj T*
(     consolation out of the offertory with--"Look, what he layeth) Tj T*
(     out, it shall be paid him again." Comfortable words, indeed,) Tj T*
(     and good to set against the old royalty of Largesse--) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(        "Whose moste joie was, I wis,) Tj T*
(        When that she gave, and said, 'Have this.'") Tj T*
() Tj T*
(     Again: the first root of the word faith being far away) Tj T*
(     in----\(compare my note on this force of it in "Modern) Tj T*
(     Painters," vol. v., p. 255\), the Latins, as proved by) Tj T*
(     Cicero's derivation of the word, got their "facio," also) Tj T*
(     involved in the idea; and so the word, and the world with) Tj T*
(     it, gradually lose themselves in an arachnoid web of) Tj T*
(     disputation concerning faith and works, no one ever taking) Tj T*
(     the pains to limit the meaning of the term: which in) Tj T*
(     earliest Scriptural use is as nearly as possible our English) Tj T*
(     "obedience." Then the Latin "fides," a quite different word,) Tj T*
(     alternately active and passive in different uses, runs into) Tj T*
(     "foi;" "facere," through "ficare," into "fier," at the end) Tj T*
(     of words; and "fidere," into "fier" absolute; and out of) Tj T*
(     this endless reticulation of thought and word rise still) Tj T*
(     more finely reticulated theories concerning salvation by) Tj T*
(     faith--the things which the populace expected to be saved) Tj T*
(     from, being indeed carved for them in a very graphic manner) Tj T*
(     in their cathedral porches, but the things they were) Tj T*
(     expected to believe being carved for them not so clearly.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(     Lastly I debated with myself whether to make the note on) Tj T*
(     Homer longer by examining the typical meaning of the) Tj T*
(     shipwreck of Ulysses, and his escape from Charybdis by help) Tj T*
ET
